{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_router", "label": "Router (local pool router)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Routees are children of the router actor, created when it is spawned and supervised by it. Five one-shot factories - roundRobin, random, broadcast, smallestMailbox, custom - each returning an ActorFactory you spawn like any other actor, with the routee's type parameter flowing through."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_routerspawnsequence", "label": "What happens at spawn time", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "## What happens at spawn time", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One RouterActor is created at the path you gave; its preStart spawns `size` children named routee-1..N and watches each so it can react if one stops."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_broadcastwrapper", "label": "Broadcast<T> message wrapper", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "## `Broadcast` - override the strategy per-message", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wraps a payload; the router unwraps it, ignores the strategy and sends the inner message to every routee. For occasional fan-out (cache invalidation, schema-update notifications) that does not fit the routine pattern. Note it fans out the RAW message including any reply-to ref, so the caller sees N replies."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_smallestmailboxrouter", "label": "Router.smallestMailbox", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "## `Router.smallestMailbox` - balance by backlog", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each message goes to the routee with the shortest queue. Three things before switching the default: it costs a depth read per routee per message against round-robin's one modulo, ties rotate so an idle pool does not pin routee-1, and the strategy never refuses to route - what happens to a message that does not fit is the mailbox's own overflow policy. Local only, because mailbox depth is in-process state."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_routercustom", "label": "Router.custom", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "## `Router.custom` - bring your own strategy", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Takes a RoutingStrategy of your own; an empty iterable means drop this message, silently and with no dead-letter routing."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_routingstrategytype", "label": "RoutingStrategy (local)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "## `Router.custom` - bring your own strategy", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "(routees, state) => Iterable<ActorRef> - one ref for single-target routing, several for fan-out, none to drop."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_stoppingthepool", "label": "Stopping the pool", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "## Stopping the pool", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stopping the router cascade-stops every routee. When a single routee stops, the router watches it and does nothing by default - its ref stays in the pool and round-robin keeps handing it roughly 1-in-N messages, which land in dead letters until the whole router restarts. Self-healing needs a restart-on-stop supervisor strategy or a BackoffSupervisor around the pool."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_sizezerobug", "label": "size = 0 is a bug", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "## Stopping the pool", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A zero-routee pool returns an empty iterable from the strategy, so every tell is dropped silently with no dead-letter routing. The framework does not validate size > 0 - the docs say it should, and until then the responsibility is the caller's."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_originalsenderpreserved", "label": "The original sender is preserved through the router", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "## Stopping the pool", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "this.sender inside a routee is the original caller, not the router, by design - the routee should be indistinguishable from a non-routed actor."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_routeeoptions", "label": "Per-routee ActorOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "## Where to next", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "withSupervisorStrategy, withDispatcher and the rest apply to routees individually via the routee options argument."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_routerspawnsequence", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_broadcastwrapper", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_smallestmailboxrouter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_routercustom", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_routercustom", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_routingstrategytype", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_stoppingthepool", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_stoppingthepool", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_sizezerobug", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_originalsenderpreserved", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_routeeoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_scatter_gather_scattergather", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_smallestmailboxrouter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_strategies_smallestmailbox", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "## `Router.smallestMailbox` - balance by backlog", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_routingstrategytype", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_strategies_routingstrategy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "## Where to next", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_router", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_pool_vs_group_poolvsgroup", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx", "source_location": "## Spawning the routees yourself", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_router_stoppingthepool", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_routing_overview_routersandsupervision", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/routing/router.mdx